 "name": "set_media_cursor",
 "description": "Attaches, moves or removes a screen recording's cursor file — the .fjcursor Frame Job writes beside each recorded movie, from which it draws the pointer, its clicks and its path — the Media tab's Cursor section ▸ Locate… (undo \"Locate Cursor File\") and Remove (\"Remove Cursor File\"). cursor is {path, bookmark?, in_picture}, the media's cursor as get_project shows it, or null to forget the file (the file itself is kept). The file is checked as Locate… checks it: it must open as a cursor file, its movie_size must be the movie's width × height, and in_picture must be the file's own (true when the movie's picture already shows the pointer), each refused in its own sentence. Refused too: an empty path, and a media that is not a video with a picture. Consolidate Media copies the file into the package beside its movie, and opening a moved package finds it there.",
 "inputSchema": {
